#
# Conformance case: teleology/maintenance-fail-vs-open-window (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# A maintenance goal that FAILS midway through a path (the safe situation drops out before the path ends) → Violated + Completed; AND a second maintenance goal whose situation still holds at every observed state and whose window is NOT yet closed → Satisfied + GoalEvaluationUndetermined (the open-window distinction — holding-so-far is not conclusive).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/maintenance-fail-vs-open-window/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
